 "result": "They're werkzeug `LocalProxy` objects backed by a single `ContextVar`.\n\n- **`src/tessel/globals.py`**: defines `_app_var: ContextVar[AppContext]` (`\"tessel.app_ctx\"`). Each global is a `werkzeug.local.LocalProxy` over that var:\n  - `app_ctx` is the `AppContext` itself.\n  - `active_app` is its `.app` attribute (the `Tessel` instance).\n  - `g` is its `.g` attribute (`_AppCtxGlobals`).\n  - `request` is its `.request` attribute (`Request`).\n  - `session` is its `.session` attribute.\n- **`src/tessel/ctx.py`**: `AppContext` pushes itself with `_app_var.set(self)` (around line 433) and stores the token in `_cv_token`. On pop it calls `_app_var.reset(self._cv_token)` (around line 498).\n\nEvery access resolves the current `AppContext` from the context var and then reads the relevant attribute. If no context is set, `LocalProxy` raises the `unbound_message` error, \"Working outside of application/request context\".\n\nThe request context has been merged into `AppContext`. `request_ctx` is only a deprecated alias for `app_ctx`.",
